Aerie-Purpose: Make the page card follow the Aerie sidebar with a transform when it shows or hides, with the card's new bounds in one step.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/ui/views/frame (vertical_tab_strip_region_view.*)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #215 (item 5 of the rest of #177). The logic is in the overlay (AerieSidebarCardFollow, chrome/browser/ui/views/aerie_sidebar);
these hooks only call it. The region view watches the contents card (the multi contents view) and arms the follower in
OnAerieVisibleChanged before the layout that moves the card; the follower starts a transform animation from the distance the card's
edge moved. Reduced motion never arms it, so the card snaps.

A show already gave the page its room in one step. A hide used to hold the room until the slide had ended; now it gives it at once
(aerie_hide_sliding_: preferred and minimum width 0) and Layout keeps the column's content at its old width, outside the region's
own bounds, so the column slides out over the room the card is taking. When the slide ends the column leaves the layout as before.

